you have XYZ that provides a part of what you want. You are debating
     whether to beat this into giving you the test

     	     VS
     reconstructing everything from scratch (which means ignoring the part of XYZ that already serves your need)


My opinion:

 Its not a str8 win for reuse sometimes beating an existing product can be more difficult than reconstructing the 
 part it provides and adding the things you need in the way you want.

 Example sm2 and maven. Beating maven to do what we need is more difficult than constructing it from scratch in Java
 and adding the part that we really do need from Maven viz., parsing a file and doing nested includes/excludes

Keep this in mind, weight the cost of rewriting common part vs adding new functionality into an existing product.

